    <string name="str_dummy_info_msg">The \'dummy\' flashrom programmer is a virtual simulator.\n\nIt does NOT use real USB hardware.\n\nValid chips to emulate (v1.7.0):\n\n• VARIABLE_SIZE — Custom size (uses size=N)\n• W25Q128.V — 16 MB\n• MX25L6405D — 8 MB\n• SST25VF032B — 4 MB\n• SST25VF040 — 512 KB\n• M25P10.RES — 128 KB\n• S25FL128L — 16 MB\n\nExample of correct command:\nflashrom -p dummy:emulate=VARIABLE_SIZE,size=16777216,image=bios_test.bin -r read_test.bin\n\n⚠ DO NOT use real chip names (e.g., W25Q128) in emulate if they differ. Only the ones listed above are valid.\n\nFor real hardware, use the appropriate programmer:\n• CH341A → ch341a_spi\n• FT2232H → ft2232_spi\n• ST-Link → stlinkv3_spi</string>
