    <string name="str_about_html">&lt;h2&gt;Flash SPI Tool&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Advanced application for reading, verifying, and writing Firmware in &lt;b&gt;SPI Flash Memories&lt;/b&gt; using the native &lt;b&gt;flashrom&lt;/b&gt; engine.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Memory and Chip Compatibility&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;✔ Supported Chips:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;SPI Flash Memories (25xx series):&lt;/b&gt; Winbond (W25Q, W25X), Macronix (MX25L), GigaDevice (GD25Q), Spansion/Cypress (S25FL), EON (EN25), etc.&lt;br/&gt;• SPI, LPC, FWH, and MTD bus chips officially supported by flashrom.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;❌ Unsupported Memories (24C series I2C EEPROMs):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• The &lt;b&gt;24C series EEPROMs&lt;/b&gt; (24C02, 24C04, 24C08, 24C16, 24C32, 24C64, 24C128, 24C256, etc.) use the &lt;b&gt;I2C&lt;/b&gt; protocol (2 wires: SDA and SCL), not SPI.&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;flashrom&lt;/b&gt; operates exclusively on the SPI bus via the &lt;code&gt;ch341a_spi&lt;/code&gt; driver and &lt;b&gt;does not support the I2C protocol&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;br/&gt;• Furthermore, 24C EEPROMs lack a universal electronic identification command (JEDEC ID 0x9F), which is why chip detection will always report that the IC was not detected.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;&lt;h3&gt;CH341A Programmer Configuration&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Programmer Mode (Jumper on pins 1-2):&lt;/b&gt; Required for the app to recognize the device as a USB programmer (VID 0x1A86, PID 0x5512). In this mode, the SPI interface operates for the 25xx series.&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;Serial TTL/UART Mode (Jumper on pins 2-3):&lt;/b&gt; The hardware switches to COM serial port mode (PID 0x5523) and will not work for programming Flash memories.&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;ZIF Socket:&lt;/b&gt; Even though the physical CH341A board has silk-screened markings for 24xx and 25xx, with this app, chips must only be inserted into the &lt;b&gt;25 SPI FLASH&lt;/b&gt; section.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Licenses and Open Source Libraries&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Project License:&lt;/b&gt; GNU GPLv3.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Dependencies and Libraries:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;a href=\"https://github.com/flashrom/flashrom\"&gt;flashrom&lt;/a&gt; (GPL-2.0)&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;a href=\"https://github.com/mik3y/usb-serial-for-android\"&gt;usb-serial-for-android&lt;/a&gt; (MIT)&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;a href=\"https://github.com/libusb/libusb\"&gt;libusb&lt;/a&gt; (LGPL-2.1+)&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;a href=\"https://github.com/pciutils/pciutils\"&gt;pciutils&lt;/a&gt; (GPL-2.0+)&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;a href=\"https://developer.intra2net.com/git/libftdi\"&gt;libftdi&lt;/a&gt; (LGPL-2.1+)&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;a href=\"https://gitlab.zapb.de/libjaylink/libjaylink\"&gt;libjaylink&lt;/a&gt; (GPL-2.0+)&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Contributors &amp; Special Thanks:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;b&gt;fsvip&lt;/b&gt; — CH347F / CH347 hardware specifications and testing&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Developer Related Projects:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• &lt;a href=\"https://github.com/Danielk10/PIC-k150-Programing\"&gt;PIC k150 Programming&lt;/a&gt; — PIC programmer via Android with P018A protocol&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</string>
